WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.550
England's Active Lives survey
tracks who is physically active,

2
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.270
and who is not.

3
00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:12.250
In the year to November 2025, 73.2 per cent
of the most affluent adults were active.

4
00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:16.070
For the least affluent,
it was 53.8 per cent.

5
00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:20.910
Money buys gym membership,
equipment, transport and holidays.

6
00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:23.130
So is money the whole story?

7
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:27.030
In this mission, you'll use the survey's
figures to measure gaps in percentage

8
00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:29.450
points, and compare their size.

9
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:34.450
Then you'll test what else might matter,
from a review of 39 studies on high-risk

10
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:38.570
sport to a model of how
tourists choose places.

11
00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:43.550
Your mission: decide whether money
alone explains who takes part in sport.
